<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The widget's metadata (issue 5.5; §35).

  Why:  `updatePeriodMillis="0"` is the load-bearing line. The system's own update alarm is capped
        at 30 minutes, cannot be tightened, wakes the device on its own schedule, and would race
        the refresh path this feature actually uses. WorkManager drives every update instead
        (`WidgetRefreshWorker`, 6-hourly plus one on each app launch), which is idempotent, honours
        the app lock, and needs no network (P-04). Zero here means "never ask me on a timer".

        `configure` is deliberately absent: there is nothing to configure. One profile, two figures.
        `targetCellWidth`/`targetCellHeight` carry `tools:ignore="UnusedAttribute"`. They are read
        only on API 31+ and the minimum here is 26, which is what Lint reports — but they are
        *additive*, not conditional: the platform's own guidance is to declare the dp size and the
        cell size together, and the older launcher simply ignores the pair rather than failing.
        Dropping them would cost correct sizing on every modern launcher; splitting them into an
        `xml-v31/` copy would make two files say the same thing.

        `initialLayout` is Glance's own placeholder — the frame the launcher shows for the moment
        between the widget being dropped and the first compose. Hand-writing one would be a second
        layout to keep in step with the real content for no visible gain.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:ignore="UnusedAttribute"
    android:description="@string/widget_description"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/glance_default_loading_layout"
    android:minWidth="180dp"
    android:minHeight="70dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="3"
    android:targetCellHeight="1"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
